# Web-specific ignores. Anything repo-wide — node_modules, out, .env, *.local.md, editor and OS
# noise — is in the root .gitignore and is not repeated here.

# build
.next/
# Where `npm run build:check` puts a build so it cannot clobber a running dev server.
.next-check/
build/
dist/

# package managers
.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/install-state.gz

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# test and tooling output
coverage/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.eslintcache
.turbo/

# deployment
.vercel

# The licensed heading face. Satoshi is Fontshare-licensed and free to redistribute, so it stays
# tracked; Beautifully Delicious Sans (Elena Genova, My Creative Land) is bought per-licence, and
# the webfont licence covers serving it from our own origin — not handing the file to everyone who
# clones a public repo. It is ignored by exact name rather than by *.woff2 so that dropping a free
# face into this directory still gets committed by default, and so that forgetting to ignore the
# next licensed one is a deliberate act rather than an oversight.
#
# Consequence, stated plainly because it will bite a fresh clone: `next build` throws
# "Can't resolve './fonts/BeautifullyDeliciousSans-Black.woff2'" until someone with the licence
# supplies the file. That is the intended failure — a missing licensed font should stop a build,
# not silently fall back to system-ui and ship a different-looking site. See app/fonts.ts.
app/fonts/BeautifullyDeliciousSans-Black.woff2
